<Layout title="Privacy Policy — Plant Identifier" description="How Plant Identifier handles uploaded photos, technical data and analytics." canonicalPath="/privacy-policy/">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Privacy policy</p><h1>Privacy, in plain language.</h1><p>Last updated: August 18, 2026</p></div></section>
  <section class="section-tight"><div class="container prose"><h2>Plant photos</h2><p>Photos you submit are processed in memory and forwarded to our identification provider to produce a result. We do not intentionally store permanent copies, publish them or create public photo URLs. Temporary processing may occur within our hosting and provider infrastructure.</p><h2>Technical information</h2><p>Our infrastructure may process IP address, request time, browser details and operational logs to deliver the site, prevent abuse, enforce usage limits and diagnose errors. We do not send image contents to analytics products.</p><h2>Third-party processing</h2><p>Identification photos are sent to Pl@ntNet under its applicable privacy and service terms. Hosting and security may be provided by Cloudflare.</p><h2>Analytics and future advertising</h2><p>We may use privacy-conscious traffic measurement to understand site use. If advertising or additional analytics are introduced, this policy and any required consent controls will be updated first.</p><h2>Your questions</h2><p>Contact <a href="mailto:hello@plantidentifier.online">hello@plantidentifier.online</a> for privacy questions.</p></div></section>
</Layout>
